menu "Synora"

    config SYNORA_MQTT_BROKER_URI
        string "MQTT broker URI (device<->server link)"
        default "wss://synora.id.vn/mqtt"
        help
            Real hardware on the public internet can't resolve
            docker-compose's "mosquitto" service name or reach its port 1883
            directly, so this rides MQTT-over-WebSocket through the same
            Traefik+Cloudflare HTTPS path already used for the REST API
            (mosquitto.conf's websockets listener, traefik/dynamic.yml's
            "mqtt" router) rather than needing separate raw-TCP exposure.
            Shared static credentials for now (see SYNORA_MQTT_USERNAME/
            PASSWORD below) -- per-device MQTT credentials are a future
            hardening item, matching the BLE always-on control path's own
            pending LE Secure Connections TODO.

    config SYNORA_MQTT_USERNAME
        string "MQTT username"
        default "synora_device"

    config SYNORA_MQTT_PASSWORD
        string "MQTT password"
        default ""
        help
            Must match docker-compose.yml's MQTT_PASSWORD env var. Left empty
            by default on purpose -- set via `idf.py menuconfig` or a
            sdkconfig.local override, never committed.

endmenu
